            <ArticleTitle>Spinal epidural lipomatosis. Case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>354-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spinal epidural lipomatosis (SEL) is a condition in which excess adipose tissue is deposited circumferentially about the spinal cord in the epidural space. It is most frequently seen in patients on chronic glucocorticosteroid therapy for a variety of medical problems. This is a case report of lumbar epidural lipomatosis in a bodybuilder with radiculopathy supposedly induced by anabolic steroid intake.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
